<title>USA: P&amp;G says returns to unisex diapers.</title>
<headline>P&amp;G says returns to unisex diapers.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Procter &amp; Gamble Co said all its Pampers disposable diapers are now unisex.</p>
<p>The company said &quot;advanced dryness technology&quot; eliminates the need for the gender-specific models introduced several years ago.</p>
<p>Pampers Baby-Dry, the new version, and Pampers Premium, introduced earlier -- a &quot;breathable&quot; diaper that is also unisex -- are both available in large-count packages, Procter &amp; Gamble said in a statement.</p>
<p>P&amp;G introduced Pampers 35 years ago.</p>
<p>-- Cleveland Newsdesk, 216-579-0077</p>
